  "configuration_id": "config_039",
  "reason": "The best result so far is config_038 (multimodal, scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, multiprofile, transformer, concat) at 0.7207 acc, which substantially outperforms the best RNA-only result (config_006, 0.6530 acc) and confirms that the image modality provides complementary signal despite its very low standalone accuracy (~0.23). The key remaining uncertainty is whether the fusion strategy matters: concat simply appends modality features, while weighted fusion lets the model learn adaptive modality importance. Config_039 is identical to config_038 except fusion changes from concat to weighted, giving a clean single-variable A/B comparison. This is the most informative next step because it directly exploits the strongest evidence, isolates the effect of one design decision (fusion), and will clarify whether the image modality's contribution is best captured by fixed concatenation or learned weighting—information that will guide all subsequent multimodal experiments."
}

